 of the liver</title><p>Tetsuro Sohda<sup>1</sup>, Takayuki Hanano<sup>1</sup>, Hisanori Miyamoto<sup>1</sup>, Yoko Kitano<sup>1</sup>, Kaoru Iwata<sup>1</sup>, Masanori Yokoyama<sup>1</sup>, Makoto Irie<sup>1</sup>, Yasuaki Takeyama<sup>1</sup>, Satoshi Shakado<sup>1</sup> and Shotaro Sakisaka<sup>1</sup></p><p>10.1007/s12072-008-9072-3</p><p>(1) Department of Gastroenterology and Medicine, Fukuoka University School of Medicine, 7-45-1 Nanakuma, Jonan-ku, Fukuoka 814-0180, Japan</p></sec><sec id="Sec2"><title>Updates in the pathogenesis, diagnosis and management of ectopic varices</title><p>Ahmed Helmy<sup>1,2</sup>, Khalid Al Kahtani<sup>2</sup> and Mohamed Al Fadda<sup>2</sup></p><p>10.1007/s12072-008-9074-1</p><p>(1) Department of Gastroenterology and Tropical Medicine, Faculty of Medicine, Assiut University Hospital, Assiut, Egypt</p><p>(2) Section of Gastroenterology, Department of Medicine, King Faisal Specialist Hospital &#x00026; Research Centre (KFSH&#x00026;RC), MBC 46, P.O. Box&#x000a0;3354, Riyadh 11211, Saudi Arabia</p></sec><sec id="Sec3"><title>Hepatocellular adenoma: what is new in 2008</title><p>Paulette Bioulac-Sage<sup>1</sup>, Herv&#x000e9; Laumonier<sup>2</sup>, Christophe Laurent<sup>3</sup>, Jessica Zucman-Rossi<sup>4</sup> and Charles Balabaud<sup>5</sup></p><p>10.1007/s12072-008-9075-0</p><p>(1) Department of Pathology, H&#x000f4;pital Pellegrin CHU Bordeaux, Universit&#x000e9; Bordeaux 2, Inserm 889, Bordeaux Cedex, France</p><p>(2) Department of Radiology, H&#x000f4;pital St Andr&#x000e9; CHU Bordeaux, Bordeaux Cedex, France</p><p>(3) Department of Surgery, H&#x000f4;pital St Andr&#x000e9; CHU Bordeaux, Bordeaux Cedex, France</p><p>(4) Inserm U674, Paris, France</p><p>(5) Department of Hepatology, H&#x000f4;pital St Andr&#x000e9; CHU Bordeaux, Universit&#x000e9; Bordeaux 2, Inserm 889, Bordeaux Cedex, France</p></sec><sec id="Sec4"><title>The effect of iron depletion on chronic hepatitis C virus infection</title><p>Massimo Franchini<sup>1</sup>, Giovanni Targher<sup>2</sup>, Franco Capra<sup>3</sup>, Martina Montagnana<sup>4</sup> and Giuseppe Lippi<sup>4</sup></p><p>10.1007/s12072-008-9076-z</p><p>(1) Servizio di Immunoematologia e Trasfusione, Centro Emofilia, Azienda Ospedaliera di Verona, Ospedale Policlinico, Piazzale Ludovico Scuro, Verona 37134, Italy</p><p>(2) Sezione di Endocrinologia e Malattie del Metabolismo, Dipartimento di Scienze Biomediche e Chirurgiche, Universit&#x000e0; di Verona, Verona, Italy</p><p>(3) Medicina Interna C, Dipartimento di Scienze Biomediche e Chirurgiche, Universit&#x000e0; di Verona, Verona, Italy</p><p>(4)   Instituto di Chimica e Microscopia Clinica, Dipartimento di Scienze Morfologico-Biomediche, Universit&#x000e0; di Verona, Verona, Italy</p></sec><sec id="Sec5"><title>Nitric oxide levels in chronic liver disease patients with and without oesophageal varices</title><p>Assem M. El-Sherif<sup>1</sup>, Mohamed A. Abou-Shady<sup>1</sup>, Ashraf M. Al-Bahrawy<sup>1</sup>, Reda M. Bakr<sup>1</sup> and Abdel-Moneim M. Hosny<sup>2</sup></p><p>10.1007/s12072-008-9077-y</p><p>(1) Internal Medicine Department, Al-Azhar Faculty of Medicine, Nasr City, Cairo, Egypt</p><p>(2) Clinical Pathology Department, Al-Azhar Faculty of Medicine, Nasr City, Cairo, Egypt</p></sec><sec id="Sec6"><title>Acute fatal presentation of ornithine transcarbamylase deficiency in a previously healthy male</title><p>Ophir D. Klein<sup>1,2</sup>, Dana R. Kostiner<sup>2,3</sup>, Kara Weisiger<sup>2</sup>, Ellen Moffatt<sup>4</sup>, Neal Lindeman<sup>4</sup>, Stephen Goodman<sup>5</sup>, Mendel Tuchman<sup>6</sup> and Seymour Packman<sup>2</sup></p><p>10.1007/s12072-008-9078-x</p><p>(1) Departments of Orofacial Sciences and Pediatrics, and Institute of Human Genetics, University of California San Francisco, 513 Parnassus Ave., Box&#x000a0;0442, San Francisco, CA 94143, USA</p><p>(2) Department of Pediatrics, Division of Medical Genetics, University of California San Francisco, San Francisco, CA, USA</p><p>(3) Present address: Departments of Medical Genetics and Internal Medicine, Kaiser Permanente Medical Center, San Francisco, USA</p><p>(4) Department of Pathology, University of California San Francisco, San Francisco, CA, USA</p><p>(5) University of Colorado School of Medicine/The Children&#x02019;s Hospital, Denver, CO, USA</p><p>(6) Children&#x02019;s Research Institute, Children&#x02019;s National Medical Center, Washington, DC, USA</p></sec><sec id="Sec7"><title>Asian-Pacific consensus statement on the management of chronic hepatitis B: a 2008 update</title><p>Yun-Fan Liaw<sup>1</sup>, Nancy Leung<sup>2</sup>, Jia-Horng Kao<sup>3</sup>, Teerha Piratvisuth<sup>4</sup>, Edward Gane<sup>5</sup>, Kwang-Hyub Han<sup>6</sup>, Richard Guan<sup>7</sup>, George K. K. Lau<sup>8</sup>, Stephen Locarnini<sup>9</sup> and for the Chronic Hepatitis B Guideline Working Party of the Asian-Pacific Association for the Study of the Liver</p><p>10.1007/s12072-008-9080-3</p><p>(1) Liver Research Unit, Chang Gung University and Memorial Hospital, 199, Tung Hwa North Road, Taipei, Taiwan</p><p>(2) Department of Medicine, Alice Ho Miu Ling Nethersole Hospital, Room 65, J6, 11 Chuen On Road, Taipo, NT, Hong Kong</p><p>(3) Hepatitis Research Center, National Taiwan University Hospital, 7 Chung-Shan South Road, Taipei 100, Taiwan</p><p>(4) NKC Institute of Gastroenterology and Hepatology, Songklanagarind Hospital, Prince of Songkla University, Hat Yai 90110, Thailand</p><p>(5) NZ Liver Transplant Unit, Auckland, New Zealand</p><p>(6) Department of Internal Medicine, Yonsei University College of Medicine, Liver Cirrhosis Clinical Research Center, Seoul, Korea</p><p>(7) Mount Elizabeth Medical Centre and National University Hospital Singapore, 3 Mt Elizabeth, #17-02, Singapore 228570, Singapore</p><p>(8) Department of Medicine, The University of Hong Kong, Room 1838, Block K, Queen Mary Hospital, 102 Pokfulum Road, Hong Kong SAR, China</p><p>(9) Research &#x00026; Molecular Development, Victorian Infectious Diseases Reference Laboratory, WHO Collaborating Centre for Virus Reference &#x00026; Research, 10 Wreckyn Street, North Melbourne, VIC 3051, Australia</p></sec><sec id="Sec8"><title>Combination therapy of lamivudine and adefovir in Japanese patients with chronic hepatitis B</title><p>Satoshi Shakado<sup>1,2</sup>, Hiroshi Watanabe<sup>1</sup>, Takashi Tanaka<sup>1,2</sup>, Daisuke Morihara<sup>1,2</sup>, Shinya Nishizawa<sup>1,2</sup>, Shinjiro Inomata<sup>1</sup>, Syuichi Ueda<sup>1</sup>, Teruo Matsumoto<sup>1</sup>, Akira Anan<sup>1,2</sup>, Yasuaki Takeyama<sup>1</sup>, Makoto Irie<sup>1</sup>, Kaoru Iwata<sup>1</sup>, Tetsuro Sohda<sup>1</sup> and Shotaro Sakisaka<sup>1,2</sup></p><p>10.1007/s12072-008-9081-2</p><p>(1) The Department of Gastroenterology and Hepatology, Fukuoka University School of Medicine, 7-45-1 Nanakuma, Jonan-ku, Fukuoka 814-0180, Japan</p><p>(2) The Division of Advanced Clinical Research for Viral Hepatitis and Liver Cancer, Fukuoka University School of Medicine, 7-45-1 Nanakuma, Jonan-ku, Fukuoka 814-0180, Japan</p></sec></body><back><fn-group><fn><p>The online version of the original article can be found under doi:10.1007/s12072-008-9072-3, 10.1007/s12072-008-9074-1, 10.1007/s12072-008-9075-0, 10.1007/s12072-008-9076-z, 10.1007/s12072-008-9077-y, 10.1007/s12072-008-9078-x, 10.1007/s12072-008-9080-3, 10.1007/s12072-008-9081-2.</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>